# .graphifyignore — code-only knowledge graph for the voice-agent platform.
# Layered on top of .gitignore (graphify respects both; gitignore last-match-wins).
#
# Goal: build the graph from CODE only (no docs / images / papers), so no LLM
# API key is required ("A code-only corpus needs no key").
#
# Extension sets are graphify's own classifications (detect.py):
#   DOC_EXTENSIONS   = .md .mdx .qmd .txt .rst .html .yaml .yml
#   IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = .png .jpg .jpeg .gif .webp .svg
#   PAPER_EXTENSIONS = .pdf
#   (CODE_EXTENSIONS — .py .ts .tsx .js .jsx .json .sh .sql .tf … — NOT excluded)

# ─── Exclude ALL doc / image / paper extensions (anywhere in the tree) ───
# Docs (graphify classifies these as documents)
*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
*.txt
*.rst
*.html
*.yaml
*.yml
# Images
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.PNG
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.GIF
*.WEBP
*.SVG
# Papers
*.pdf
*.PDF

# ─── Exclude vendored AI-tooling skill packs (their CODE, not the platform) ───
# These contain real .ts/.tsx/.py/.sh files (web-artifacts-builder mockup,
# pdf/xlsx scripts, mermaid scripts) that would pollute a platform code graph.
.claude/
.codex/
.cline/

# ─── Exclude scratch / generated non-code dirs ───
.docs/
worker/.docs/
e2e/reports/
